# Stdlib → compiler compatibility manifest (issue #396).
#
# The compiler reads this BEFORE flattening the stdlib and refuses to load it
# if `requires-compiler-abi` exceeds the ABI the compiler binary was built to
# validate (src/toolchain.rs::STDLIB_ABI_VERSION). This turns a version-skew
# crash — a type error that points at the stdlib, not the skew — into one
# clear sentence.
#
# Bump this to match the compiler's STDLIB_ABI_VERSION whenever this stdlib
# starts relying on a compiler contract (extern-type whitelist, prelude shape,
# marshaling/wire encoding) that older compilers lack. See the bump rule next
# to STDLIB_ABI_VERSION in src/toolchain.rs.
requires-compiler-abi = 1
